{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling","id":891351,"title":"Convincing group to run Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-15T13:53:07-07:00","id":891351,"title":"Convincing group to run Changeling","content":"My D&amp;D group has recently been trying out different RP systems. We've done Shadowrun, Stars Without Numbers, Dungeon World ... now I want to try and get them to try WoD. I know none of us want to play Vampire, but I think Mage or Changeling could be fun. We tend to like heavy focus on the RP-aspects, lots of drama and crazy stuff. I could totally see them liking Changeling. I've never played any World of Darkness games, though, so I'm not sure how to best sell it to them, since what got me interested in both Changeling and Mage was poring over the rule books. <br /> <br /> What I'd need help with is an elevator pitch. A very brief argument as to what it'd be awesome to give Changeling a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:37:21-07:00","id":891413,"title":"","content":"Are you looking for a pitch to sell the setting or the mechanics to your group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:55:04-07:00","id":891423,"title":"","content":"From a dnd perspective: You were a mortal, a human dragged into a place of the fey (like the fey wilds) by an arch fey who reshaped you so you could survive in such a place. You were a servant to this being in some way or another until you escaped. Somehow you find your way back to the material world but a false-you is living your life and you are no longer truly mundane. By being reshaped you have been made into a minor fey with all that, that entails. So now you must decide how you will live your new life, will you take back your old life or forge a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:27:54-07:00","id":891435,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's brief enough, but I tried to encompass <b><a href=\"http://www.vtm.kismetrose.com/ChangelingIntro.html\" target=\"_blank\">the highlights of the game/system here</a></b>. I wish you the best, because if they let you run it, they'll be glad they did!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:01:32-07:00","id":892041,"title":"","content":"This is a game where you can play ANY concept from any background. Want to play a furry character? Done! You're a beast. Want to play a elven knight? Done! you're a fairest Draconic. Want to play an alien? Done! You're a wizened. And it's all played in a contemporary setting. There's guns, drugs and any other drama you can come up with. There's a well defined bad guy and cool, interesting magical items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:51:30-07:00","id":892147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892041#post892041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a game where you can play ANY concept from any background. Want to play a furry character? Done! You're a beast. Want to play a elven knight? Done! you're a fairest Draconic. Want to play an alien? Done! You're a wizened. And it's all played in a contemporary setting. There's guns, drugs and any other drama you can come up with. There's a well defined bad guy and cool, interesting magical items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got that right. I've got a character who's a Glitch-mon who can hack computers by literally sweet-talking them. Got another NPC who's a high wyrd/low clarity devil gunsmith who upgrades antique firearms into magic guns. Tell him Linkara sent you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T19:13:30-07:00","id":892193,"title":"","content":"The court system is also pretty sweet, allowing you to take the flavour and history of a location and turn it into magical organizations with interesting practices rather easily, and the benefits that you can give through them can be very dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:28:31-07:00","id":892223,"title":"","content":"&quot;Imagine if Pathfinder was set in modern times, but most humans didn't know about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Can't see what's not to like about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and I have no doubt that there's a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_of_Pain\" target=\"_blank\">Lady of Pain</a> style Fey wandering around out there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-16-2016, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:42:29-07:00","id":892232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892223#post892223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Imagine if Pathfinder was set in modern times, but most humans didn't know about it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you try to do Pathfinder stuff you're likely to get thrown in gaol..... I mean, changelings can escape things really well, but being on the run from humans and on the run from Gentry at the same time doesn't sound the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:45:40-07:00","id":892235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892232#post892232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you try to do Pathfinder stuff you're likely to get thrown in gaol..... I mean, changelings can escape things really well, but being on the run from humans and on the run from Gentry at the same time doesn't sound the best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that's kind of the point of the game, you're thrown into unfortunate circumstances and now we get to see how you survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:54:43-07:00","id":892240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892235#post892235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's kind of the point of the game, you're thrown into unfortunate circumstances and now we get to see how you survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being on the run from police 100% of the time isn't exactly the point of my changeling games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T20:59:53-07:00","id":892243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892240#post892240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being on the run from police 100% of the time isn't exactly the point of my changeling games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well no, I would imagine you'd have some pretty dumb changelings if it was. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The point I was trying to make is = Supernatural creatures, pocket dimensions, practically anything you can dream up, and beings of incalculable power trying to capture and enslave you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:49:50-07:00","id":892590,"title":"","content":"I see a big difference in the tone of D&amp;D/Pathfinder and Changeling, and a lot of it is in character motivations. In D&amp;D and similar games, you're an adventurer who willingly faces danger instead of living a comparatively safe normal life. In Changeling, you're a person who's been forced into a dangerous life trying to approximate normal life. Those other games can have sessions reduced to the &quot;mindless&quot; dungeon crawl if the DM isn't up to creating a deep story. While I plan on having a few dungeon crawls (trying for a fairy tale tone, with non-grindy challenges that double as secret tests of character or the like) in the Hedge, I don't think I could reduce Changeling that easily.<br /> <br /> I guess the TL;DR version would be: &quot;In D&amp;D/etc, you're Superman. In Changeling, you're Spider-Man.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:48:32-07:00","id":892667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Razikale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling#post891351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd need help with is an elevator pitch. A very brief argument as to what it'd be awesome to give Changeling a try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Movie Trailer Voice:<br /> &quot;In a world like our own but where the shadows run deeper and supernatural beings, both familiar and beyond human comprehension, prey upon humanity, your characters are the escaped survivors who were abducted to realms of unbelievable horror and wonder past sanity, and reason by beings which dwarf human understanding. Wounded, rattled, and warped by powers beyond this world, and having removed chunks from their own psyche like a fox chewing off its foot to escape as trap, they must find support from fellow refugees of this realm,yet avoiding those that would betray them and send them back to the realms of madness, while evading the huntsmen sent by their inhuman abductors. Are these traumatized souls up for the challenge or will they be dragged back to a realm where even death isn't a release?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Chronicle of course would be the answer to the question, just like a book or movie is the answer to the question at the end of a well-written &quot;teaser&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the players seem interested in answering the ending question, they'll be interested in playing <i>Changeling: The Lost - Huntsmen Chronicles</i>.<br /> <br /> By the way, I am gearing up for a Pacific Northwest Frailty Chronicle, and when I am ready I'll post a link to my youtube channel in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 05-23-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:38:27-07:00","id":900370,"title":"","content":"For me, one of the interesting things about Changeling is the way the characters are changed. They were human, then they were slaves, now they've escaped. They don't want to go back, so they get stronger and more powerful so they can fight off the things trying to get them to go back. And in the process, become not all that dissimilar from their former masters. Seriously, the difference between a Wyrd 10 Changeling and a True Fae is pretty slim, from what I recall. Also, the idea of the Courts (at least in 1E) being how the Changelings choose to hide I thought was very interesting. Partially for the inevitable, cyclical nature of the changing seasons being incomprehensible to the True Fae, and the fact that which Court you gravitated towards meant you hid in a different manner. Everything Changelings do being a reaction to what their Keepers did to them created lots of strong, narrative potentials, and exploring these characters and what had been done to them was very interesting to me. Also, Changeling is a great game in which come up with the most horrifying backstories imaginable, and play a character trying to deal with that. The first character idea I had on reading the core book was a Darkling Mirrorskin who was essentially some &quot;mobile decoration&quot; used by his Keeper for the, eh, <i>pleasure</i> of the Keeper and anyone the Keeper wanted to, ah, <i>entertain</i>. Most other games, that kind of backstory would have people wondering what your damage is. In a game like Changeling, it's Tuesday.<br /> <br /> Changeling is also awesome because the aspect of beauty. There's a lot of awesome stuff in Arcadia, and the idea of being a True Fae, having complete control over your little corner of reality, and ability to remake it as you see fit on a whim, is pretty awesome. Of course, the True Fae use their powers in the most horrible ways, but that idea, of creating beauty in the world and changing it to suit you, can be a really uplifting one. Or a terrifying one. Or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:23:30-07:00","id":904034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=892590#post892590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the TL;DR version would be: &quot;In D&amp;D/etc, you're Superman. In Changeling, you're Spider-Man.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spiderman was considered one of the 10 strongest characters in his universe for a while, though. I think he's taken down Hulk before!<br /> <br /> Imagine if he got bitten by a radioactive dung beetle.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, I would suggest that before trying to start a game, you make sure the players know the theme of Changeling and World of Darkness in general. It's not about glorifying your characters (indeed, that would probably <i>lure the Fey</i>), but about seeing how they deal with tragedy. It's more of a psychological thriller than a fantasy adventure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:32:55-07:00","id":904039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=900370#post900370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, one of the interesting things about Changeling is the way the characters are changed. They were human, then they were slaves, now they've escaped. They don't want to go back, so they get stronger and more powerful so they can fight off the things trying to get them to go back. And in the process, become not all that dissimilar from their former masters. Seriously, the difference between a Wyrd 10 Changeling and a True Fae is pretty slim, from what I recall. Also, the idea of the Courts (at least in 1E) being how the Changelings choose to hide I thought was very interesting. Partially for the inevitable, cyclical nature of the changing seasons being incomprehensible to the True Fae, and the fact that which Court you gravitated towards meant you hid in a different manner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought it was the Courts working together that was incomprehensible. Since the True Fey are utterly selfish beings who only concern themselves with their personal desires. By forming a community together, the Changelings were able to confuse and disorient them.<br /> <br /> Only the Winter Court was described as actually hiding from the Fey. The other Courts were focused on something quite different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summer Court</b> were warriors, they did not hide.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn Court</b> were occultists, they demanded an explanation.<br /> <br /> <b>Spring Court</b> were in denial, using pleasure to numb the pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:54:11-07:00","id":904043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=904039#post904039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the Winter Court was described as actually hiding from the Fey.<br /> <br /> The other Courts were focused on something quite different.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer Court</b> were warriors, they did not hide.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn Court</b> were occultists, they demanded an explanation.<br /> <br /> <b>Spring Court</b> were in denial, using pleasure to numb the pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyr, I know you've said you only have the corebook, but it might behoove you to not then feign understanding of the setting eight books and the cusp of an edition change into the line. There is more than one way to hide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lords of Summer, p29</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why join the court of Desire? Why dress brightly and revel noisily when the hounds are on your trail? Because it\u2019s not what <u>They</u> expect. The Others are looking for what they think they\u2019ve broken, tamed, discarded or stolen every ounce of truly living away from. They\u2019re looking for something wounded and frightened. By walking in the light, laughing, loving and truly living, Spring courtiers take away their primary identifying feature. They wrap themselves in the armor of pleasure, knowing that it hides them from their former Keepers far better than any shadow ever could.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lords of Summer, p70</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Palace of Dust: Sometimes, the Autumn Court appears to be essentially absent from a freehold entirely, its presence felt only through the ripples in the passion of fear that echoes down from the changelings\u2019 hidden actions. These Lost take the court\u2019s mandate to an extreme, to be sure, but those that pull it off well are often afforded great respect (which may never end up being offered to them in person) by their fellows in the other three seasonal courts. To be clear, these fae do not hide in the manner of the Winter Court, but rather to the intended end of propagating a sense of unease among the Courts; for, who knows when an Autumn fae is watching or what frightful plans she might have in store?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:46:16-07:00","id":904071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=904043#post904043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nyr, I know you've said you only have the corebook, but it might behoove you to not then feign understanding of the setting eight books and the cusp of an edition change into the line. There is more than one way to hide.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, kind of new to role playing games that aren't in video format. Wasn't quite prepared all the supplement book content <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:07:40-07:00","id":904077,"title":"","content":"One interpretation of the Autumn court I'm thinking of using: They're not hiding, they're <i>lurking.</i> For all their power, the Gentry can be hurt and killed. The Autumn Court studies Fae magic and the Gentry so that they can instill even just a little fear in them. &quot;What if they know my frailty? What if they've figured out what I'm <i>really</i> up to?&quot; Even pretending to know more than they actually do might be enough to give the Gentry pause about appearing in the mortal world. They're like Minecraft's Creepers: They may be easy to deal with when you see them coming, but it's always the one you don't see that gets you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:47:08-07:00","id":904106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/891351-convincing-group-to-run-changeling?p=904039#post904039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought it was the Courts working together that was incomprehensible. Since the True Fey are utterly selfish beings who only concern themselves with their personal desires. By forming a community together, the Changelings were able to confuse and disorient them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little of column A, little of column B.<br /> <br /> The point I remember from the original core (also the only book I've read/own, don't feel bad) is that the True Fae can't grasp the cyclical nature of changing seasons. A Queen of Winter Fae might get bored one day and decide to become a Prince of Spring, that was on a whim, and both winter and spring last only as long as s/he wants them to. The fact that winter has a finite length, then becomes spring which has a finite length, then to summer etc., is a bit the True Fae can't quite wrap their heads around. And during each season, the appropriate Court leads the local Freehold, mirroring that change of seasons (and, if memory serves, reinforcing the Contracts Changelings have made with the seasons themselves.) Just as a True Fae can't contemplate their realm changing on a schedule they have no control over, they can't conceive of turning power over their realm to another, trusting that they'll get it back in about a year. So, yeah, little of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}